From: pointofpressure <pointofpressure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:35:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] worldgen: decoration_replay, a chunk's placed features
 replayed against a caller's view

DecorationReplay (horizon_world::worldgen::decoration_replay) gives a preset dimension's
decoration to callers outside the generator: its roots by identity, whether each runs, the
biome lists, and replay(), which runs chosen roots for one chunk and seed with the
generator's own decoration seed, feature seeds, placement chains and features, reporting each
block they would set. Nothing is written to a level; reads see earlier writes over the
caller's view. Lets a client predict what generation placed (ore finders) without
Decoration, FeaturePlacer, FeatureWorld or PlacementContext becoming public.

GeneratorData::decoration_of is prepare_decoration's lookup, shared.
